<<<
commitment, committal. In nearly all senses the two forms are interchangeable, but -tal gains ground

-ment loses it. The sense engagement, however, i.e. the being committed to doing something, be- longs almost only to -ment, & the sense perpetration, i.e. the committing of some offence, almost only to -tal.
===
**commitment, committal.** In nearly all senses the two forms are interchangeable, but *-tal* gains ground while *-ment* loses it. The sense engagement, however, i.e. the being committed to doing something, belongs almost only to *-ment*, & the sense perpetration, i.e. the committing *of* some offence, almost only to *-tal*.
>>>

